{
 "gdd": "hud-and-suit-layer",
 "blocking": [
  "States (DOWNED row, line ~938), EC-HS-24, HS-6, HS-10, HS-39, HS-41, HS-47, HS-57, Cross-References table 1 (no K43) vs player-controller-input.md lines 591, 879, 1024 and AC-PCI-024: [design-review main, confirmed by creative-director] The Player Controller's re-review gives the HUD three things to do. Line 879 names a 'single-owner DOWNED-only give_up confirm plate at the chest point', 'the non-audio ignored-input dim' and 'the first-use captions'. It also adds a new read, input_ignored_view(seat), and three of its passages tie the dim to NOT_LIT. The HUD rejects all three. Its DOWNED row at line 938 and EC-HS-24 say the give-up action 'draws nothing on the HUD'. HS-6 closes the read list, HS-10 and AC-HS-12 close the surface inventory, HS-39 keeps the chest area clear, and HS-41 with AC-HS-143 bans any dip on an unlit subject. HS-57 and OQ-HS-29 ban captions and hints at MVP. AC-PCI-024 and AC-HS-12/AC-HS-143 cannot both pass. D7 ('give up and reload') is a user ruling, so as the two documents stand that ruling cannot be built. That is the rule-1 exception, and it makes this a real blocker. Creative ruling on the three asks: (a) ACCEPT the give-up plate. It confirms the player's own input and tells them nothing about the world, so it does not touch P3. (b) ACCEPT the dim only where the press was blocked by the player's own state (MOVING). (c) REJECT the dim on NOT_LIT presses and REJECT both first-use captions. A visible response to pressing at an unlit subject tells the player something is there, which is the exact unlit-subject oracle P3 forbids. Captions break anti-pillar 4 at MVP, and teaching belongs to the world (Cryo Bay onboarding)."
 ],
 "disagreements": [
  "[creative-director vs design-review main] The main review's fix for the panel arrangement asks for 'a recommended default (the creative-director's COLUMN lean)'. I am withdrawing that lean as a default the fixers can apply. The main review itself records that COLUMN breaks the P1 rule that the upper 70% of the screen stays HUD-free (it drops to 50%, or 70.6% with a notice). A default that breaks a pillar must not be baked in by a fixer. ROW vs COLUMN must be a user decision at /ux-design, presented with the P1 cost of COLUMN against ROW's narrower offered sizes (144 px per side, H_default only on k_auto = 2 displays). Until then, compute the allocation and accessibility-ceiling numbers for both arrangements, not just one.",
  "[creative-director refines design-review main] The main fix offers to accept the ignored-input dim 'for plate-shown cases only' as one option. I rule more narrowly: the dim is allowed only for presses blocked by the player's own state (MOVING), through the existing press_blocked_moving plate dim. NOT_LIT is refused outright, even where a plate is shown. A visible response to a press at an unlit subject leaks the subject's existence, and P3 does not allow that.",
  "[creative-director vs design-review main, minor] For MARK_DUTY_PM, I prefer tightening the safe range to the feasible set over adding a duty check to the validator, because it is the simpler fix. Either fix is acceptable."
 ]
